    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d593">

                <pb facs="0762" n="688" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg688"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/6811</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reinsch</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-09-12T18:00:00+08:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 12, 1917, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received September 12, 5.10
                        p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your telegram of March 26, 4 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d593-f1"/> The Chinese
                    Foreign Office gives oral assurance that educational program of 1918 will in any
                    case be continued unchanged and promises that this assurance will <pb
                        facs="0763" n="689" xml:id="pg689"/> be formally confirmed in writing if and
                    when the United States Government announces its acceptance of postponement of
                    indemnity payments as proposed in the note of the Allied Ministers of September
                    8 as reported in my September 5, 12 p.m.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
